invariant: INV-48
file: keccak_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mlkem-avx2
reason: the start leaves out the last pad bit in byte 167, so the four
  states absorb an unpadded block. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds
  bin/mlkem_avx2_equiv_test for x86-64 and runs it under
  qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
        s->lane[20][k] = (uint64_t)0x80 << 56;
--- new
        s->lane[20][k] = 0;
